cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, together with the paper."
title: "ASDExplicitGamma: an explicit threshold for the superdiffusion renormalization induction, formalized in Lean 4"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/scottnarmstrong/ASDExplicitGamma"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the renormalization
  induction of Armstrong, Bou-Rabee and Kuusi (arXiv:2601.22142) with an
  explicit threshold: for the planar q x q Gaussian model and every
  self-similarity exponent gamma <= 17/50000, the effective diffusivity stays
  in an explicit corridor at every scale, and the homogenization error
  satisfies an explicit two-term tail bound and explicit L^p moment bounds for
  every real p >= 1. These imply the paper's induction hypothesis with the
  constant E = 2^16. The statements are about the objects of the public
  Superdiffusion formalization. The library contains no sorry and no custom
  axiom.
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
  - family-names: Kuusi
    given-names: Tuomo
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - superdiffusion
  - stochastic homogenization
  - renormalization
license: Apache-2.0
references:
